# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Unity
# Regenerated by Unity on open. Library alone is 3.3 GB here.
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# Per-user IDE / solution files, regenerated from the project.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Build products
*.apk
*.aab
*.app
*.unitypackage
crashlytics-build.properties

# macOS
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- project
# Hand-rolled backups of source files. Git is the reason these can go:
# every one of them is a previous state of a file that is now in history.
# 146 files / 6.2 MB as of the first commit.
*.bak
*.bak.meta

# Screenshots already staged for deletion (44 MB of PNGs). The device bridge
# cannot delete files, so they were moved here instead of removed.
Assets/**/.to_delete/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: Assets/Phase1/qa_*.txt and friends. Those are the
# measurement files the tuning decisions rest on - the engine ladder, the
# cascade probe, the damage sweeps - and the design docs cite them by name.

# Scratch copies made by earlier zip-delivery sessions. Each holds an OUT OF
# DATE duplicate of the real scripts (BuilderManager.cs was 2049-2196 lines in
# these; the live file is 4018), so committing them would put four editable
# stale copies of the main source file in the repo. Same reason *.bak is
# ignored: git is what these folders were standing in for.
Assets/Phase1/.bundle*/

# GitHub token, pasted by owen, read by the shell as $(cat .gh_token.local) and
# never printed. MUST stay ignored: every folder this session can reach lives
# inside this repository, so an un-ignored secret here would be one `git add -A`
# away from being pushed to a remote.
.gh_token.local

# Telegram bot token for @OwensClaudeBot, same rule as the GitHub token above:
# pasted by owen, read as $(cat .telegram_token.local), never printed. A bot
# token is a full credential - anyone holding it can read and send everything
# the bot can - so it is ignored BEFORE the file is created, not after.
.telegram_token.local
.telegram_chat.local

# scratch used to defeat the stale-file cache in device_stage_files
Assets/Phase1/.push_tmp/

# ---- 2026-08-05: kept out of the repo, with the measurement that decided it --
# The Xcode build output. 1.1 GB, entirely regenerated by a Unity build, and
# far past what belongs in source control.
ios/

# QA screenshots. 175 MB of PNGs captured by the probes; they are evidence for
# a session, not project content, and the sessions that need them write fresh
# ones. The qa_*.txt REPORTS beside them stay tracked (279 of them already are)
# because those are small, diffable, and get quoted in handovers.
Assets/Phase1/qa_shots/

# The bridge to this machine cannot delete files - rm fails with "Operation not
# permitted" - so anything that needs removing gets moved here instead and the
# owner empties it by hand. Never content.
_to_delete/

# ---- 2026-08-09: the server tree is .NET, and the Unity rules above misfire --
# Two ways, both found by reading .git/index rather than by anything failing:
#
# 1. `/[Oo]bj/` and `/[Bb]uild/` are ROOT-ANCHORED (leading slash), so they
#    never covered server/RobotBrawl.Api/obj/, and there was no bin/ rule at
#    all. The first `git add -A` after the API compiled committed 2.8 MB of
#    build output - twelve DLLs including Npgsql and the whole IdentityModel
#    stack, apphost, the compiled assembly, MSBuild caches, and
#    project.assets.json, which hard-codes /Users/leondu paths.
#
# 2. `*.csproj` is ignored because UNITY regenerates its project files. But
#    server/RobotBrawl.Api/RobotBrawl.Api.csproj is HAND-WRITTEN and is the
#    only thing that knows the API's package references. It was silently
#    excluded, so the repo held every source file, every build artifact, and
#    nothing that could build them. A fresh clone could not compile the API.
server/**/bin/
server/**/obj/
!server/**/*.csproj

# Regenerated by tests/run_local.sh on every run, full of timestamps and
# absolute paths. The qa_*.txt REPORT beside it stays tracked, per the rule
# above - a report is evidence, a log is exhaust.
server/qa_api_server.log

# ---- 2026-08-09: the Cowork <-> Claude Code CLI relay ---------------------
# A work queue between two sessions, not source. Anything in here worth
# keeping graduates to docs/ as a dated record.
_relay/
